import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Services" description="WebGIS development, spatial analysis, and GIS data automation, using open-source tools or your existing ArcGIS environment.">
  <h1>Services</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every project starts with what you need to get done. The software comes second.</p>

  <h2>WebGIS development</h2>
  <p>
    Web maps and dashboards for sharing data with staff, partners, or the public. Open-source apps
    can be hosted as static sites at little or no cost. In ArcGIS, I build with Experience Builder,
    dashboards, and Field Maps for data collection.
  </p>

  <h2>Spatial analysis</h2>
  <p>
    Analysis to answer planning and program questions: where needs are greatest, which sites are
    most suitable, and how conditions have changed over time. You get maps ready for reports or
    grant applications, along with a plain-language explanation of the methods.
  </p>

  <h2>Data cleanup and automation</h2>
  <p>
    Python scripts and tools that clean messy spreadsheets and shapefiles, geocode addresses, and
    keep datasets updated on a schedule, using open-source libraries or ArcPy.
  </p>

  <h2>Working in your ArcGIS organization</h2>
  <p>
    If you already have ArcGIS Online or ArcGIS Enterprise, I can work as a member of your
    organization, so your maps, apps, and data stay in your account from day one.
  </p>

  <h2>How projects work</h2>
  <p>
    We start with a short call about what you need. I then send a written scope with a fixed price,
    so you know the cost before any work begins.
  </p>
  <p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a></p>
</Base>
